<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Ditch</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>ditch &lt;player&gt;
</pre>
<p>Stops a player from following you; they are told that you ditched them. 
They don't need to be in the same room: you can ditch a follower anywhere 
in the world. It works only on players. A monster that follows you, such 
as a charmed animal or one of your undead, can't be ditched this way.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Follow</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Group</a>
</pre>




</div>